{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book","id":3053,"title":"The Long Journey: what do you want to see in Promethean's Chronicle book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T17:44:00-08:00","id":3053,"title":"The Long Journey: what do you want to see in Promethean's Chronicle book?","content":"What it says in the title. Who or what should be the default \u201cplot drivers\u201d of the setting (e.g., the God-Machine, the Strix, the Idigam, the Fallen World\u2026)? How should the rules be updated? Some of my own thoughts:<br /> <br /> Given the game's focus on learning about humanity and striving to achieve Mortality, I think the default plot drivers should be humans: e.g., <b>The Long Journey: the Mortal Chronicle</b>. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Humanity should be reworked to start at 3 and build up from there, with higher levels of Humanity making the Promethean <i>physically</i> more human as well as <i>mentally</i> more human.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Lineages should be generalized to Humours, with the existing Lineages being retained as customizations of Humours, much like how Kiths customize Seemings in <b>Changeling</b>.<br /> \u2022 Athanors should be based on Refinements instead of Lineages.<br /> \u2022 Get rid of the ranking system for Transmutations. Handle them more like Embeds in <b>Demon</b>.<br /> \u2022 Include a box addressing if and how the Principle and its <i>qashmallim </i>differ from the God-Machine and its angels.<br /> \u2022 Revise Disquiet, preferably to interact with the Integrity of significant mortal characters (and with \u201cmook rules\u201d when dealing with characters who are individually unimportant). By default, assume that other supernaturals are immune to Disquiet, but give the Storyteller the option to have Disquiet interact with other supernaturals in their own way.<br /> \u2022 Revise Wasteland to streamline it, and to tie it more to use of Pyros in an area rather than merely the passage of time; address the question of if and how Wastelands recover as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-04-2013, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T21:16:25-08:00","id":3146,"title":"","content":"How would the Zeka be handled if Lineages are all truncated into Humours? Would it just be like it is now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T21:54:19-08:00","id":3166,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, yeah: the Zeka would have a &quot;Nuclear&quot; Humour, where they're defined more by the (nuclear) contamination than by any particular bodily fluid. The variety of possible Nuclear Bestowments would map to individual Lineages, as would the multiple Progenitors that <b>Saturnine Night</b> describes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T04:58:16-08:00","id":3368,"title":"","content":"I don;t want a Qashmallim chronicle - I love those freaky angels, but 90% of the time (whether they're a messenger or harbinger of doom) they're walking, talking, burning plot device. They also have a lot of similarity with angels and demons, now. Them being reworked as a primary focus rather than a fringe weirdness would weaken Promethean, IMO.<br /> <br /> I want Pandorans expanded and made a bit nastier - Dormacy should work a bit like the Weeping Angels, perhaps, and there should be ways for Pandorans to ijteract with humans and endure long periods of starvation without turning into stone - Prometheans are a <i>rare</i> food source. I have no idea how the Lady of Chains manages.<br /> <br /> I agree 100% on Transmutations being more like Embeds/Exalted Charms. Humanity starting at 3, well, that's just common sense.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have supernaturals immune to Disquiet at all though, especially mages (arguably the most human of the bunch). While I approve of weakening Wastelands (though I favour an Azoth-based system where Azoth 1 Prometheans ruin a few rooms and Azoth 10 Prometheans potentially blight entire cities - it's simpler, slower and harder to avoid than a Pyros-based system) Disquiet shouldn't have its teeth pulled.<br /> <br /> I like your Seeming/Kith idea... but I adore the Lineages. I really do. I think your 'kith' axis should be why the Promethean was made. because as it stands the Lineages are arguably more distinct by their intended purpose rather than their humour (except the Zeka); Galateids were made to be ideal lovers, Osirans to replace someone that was lost, the Tammuz to be slaves, the Ulgan to be a medium between worlds, Frankensteins to see if it could be done and Zeka.... because radioactivity? Using purpose and humour as your two determinants, each giving you access to different Embeds, would be a neat way of doing this that is <i>simpler</i> than making a lot of kiths and yet more customisable. Though I rather hope nobody makes a zeka for a lover...<br /> <br /> This system also fixes what I think we all see as an issues with Promethean's core, in that in has only 6 origin points for Prometheans, something every single supplement worked to undo without actually saying so - what with tons of new, unique Lineages, progenitors, weirdnesss like extempores and animal prometheans and the fact that <i>Saturnine Night</i> outright says the Zeka had at least three Demiurges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:20:17-08:00","id":3428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don;t want a Qashmallim chronicle - I love those freaky angels, but 90% of the time (whether they're a messenger or harbinger of doom) they're walking, talking, burning plot device. They also have a lot of similarity with angels and demons, now. Them being reworked as a primary focus rather than a fringe weirdness would weaken Promethean, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; that\u2019s why I didn\u2019t suggest reworking them as a primary focus. The primary focus for <b>Promethean</b> should be <i>mortal humans</i>, as seen from the outside. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Pandorans expanded and made a bit nastier - Dormacy should work a bit like the Weeping Angels, perhaps, and there should be ways for Pandorans to interact with humans and endure long periods of starvation without turning into stone - Prometheans are a <i>rare</i> food source. I have no idea how the Lady of Chains manages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have supernaturals immune to Disquiet at all though, especially mages (arguably the most human of the bunch). While I approve of weakening Wastelands (though I favour an Azoth-based system where Azoth 1 Prometheans ruin a few rooms and Azoth 10 Prometheans potentially blight entire cities - it's simpler, slower and harder to avoid than a Pyros-based system) Disquiet shouldn't have its teeth pulled.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Chronicle book itself probably isn't the right place to address crossover rules. Granting immunity to Disquiet to other supernaturals serves two purposes: first, it's short and simple: the whole of the rule can be fit in a simple, short sentence. Second, it removes the single biggest stumbling block to crossover play that exists; and in general, when you\u2019re talking about how Prometheans interact with other supernaturals, you\u2019re talking about crossover play. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your Seeming/Kith idea... but I adore the Lineages. I really do. I think your 'kith' axis should be why the Promethean was made. because as it stands the Lineages are arguably more distinct by their intended purpose rather than their humour (except the Zeka); Galateids were made to be ideal lovers, Osirans to replace someone that was lost, the Tammuz to be slaves, the Ulgan to be a medium between worlds, Frankensteins to see if it could be done and Zeka.... because radioactivity? Using purpose and humour as your two determinants, each giving you access to different Embeds, would be a neat way of doing this that is <i>simpler</i> than making a lot of kiths and yet more customisable. Though I rather hope nobody makes a zeka for a lover...</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But would you restrict a Galeteid to only making Galeteids with the generative act, or would you let her make <i>any</i> Sanguine Lineage? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This system also fixes what I think we all see as an issues with Promethean's core, in that in has only 6 origin points for Prometheans, something every single supplement worked to undo without actually saying so - what with tons of new, unique Lineages, progenitors, weirdnesss like extempores and animal prometheans and the fact that <i>Saturnine Night</i> outright says the Zeka had at least three Demiurges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five, actually.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:52:14-08:00","id":3450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3428#post3428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. But would you restrict a Galeteid to only making Galeteids with the generative act, or would you let her make <i>any</i> Sanguine Lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically, the second half of their ''type' under this model would map to the purpose they were made for. Could be made as a servant or just for the sake of reproducing. Giving them access to different affinity Embeds as well as the Sanguine Affinity Embeds/Bestowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T07:01:23-08:00","id":3457,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>I'm ok with saying supernatural creatures are immune, but I'd prefer to say their Disquiet level cannot raise beyond a number. Wasteland as Datawaver said.Transmutations as Embeds would be really fine. I'd actually want to see something similar RIGHT NOW. Humanity at 3 is the way.</li> <li>Revised qashmallim.</li> <li>I don't particularily like the Kith/Seeming thing.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T07:22:12-08:00","id":3473,"title":"","content":"I don't like supernaturals being immune to Disquiet. I'd much rather see unique effects for each template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T09:00:43-08:00","id":3540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3473#post3473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like supernaturals being immune to Disquiet. I'd much rather see unique effects for each template.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could also be a good idea. Like, Vampires might react different from mortals to Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T09:24:18-08:00","id":3562,"title":"","content":"Like, the closer a supernatural template is to human, the more disquiet affects them? I like that idea. Perhaps the effect on them rachets up with Morality traits, particularly Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:16:34-08:00","id":3674,"title":"","content":"To me my biggest priority for the Promethian Chronicle - I would call it: The Pilgramage Chroncilces - would be to try to capture the way Promethians really hate their life. I think it's a little too easy to go around thinking that you're an awesome super-being wondering the earth (how many of us would like to go on a round the world trip) with no responsibilities. Pity that everyone else is an arsehole.<br /> <br /> To that end I'd probably do two things:<br /> <br /> Firstly rename Torment to Release. Torment is the natural state for all Promethians, and the episodes where you go on a rampage are the blessed escape. I'd probably try to make you roll frequently so you notice how inescapable it is, but most rolls just accumulate Torment points that make your next episode of Release is. Fluff wise, every Promethean has a natural state that's <i>absolutely terrible</i>, for example a: Golem is an unthinking tool. Trying to be anything else, such as a Golem <i>thinking for herself</i>, is horrible. It feels unatural, dirty, like being trapped in the wrong body, etc. So every time a Golem is given an order they roll torment, eventually the stress of saying no is too much and they walk up to the nearest human and report up for duty. Disquiet builds, and when the guy forgot to tell you to stop fetching water he tries to kill you.<br /> <br /> I see the Lineages (IMO this is a Lineage not Humour thing) as:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Frankenstein - pulling in one hundred directions: Torment builds when you deny your impulses. Release makes you run around following the first idea in your head.<br /> Galataid - the perfect partner: Torment builds when you try to be yourself, not what someone else wants you to be. Release turns you into a Stepford wife, or whatever your lover wants.<br /> Osiren - Osiris: Literally. Torment builds when you show ungodly humility. Release means you think you are Osris and act like like He would.<br /> Golem - Tool: Even slaves are people, Torment builds when you try to disobey and order or follow it in anything but the most literal manner. Release turns you into an unthinking automaton.<br /> Riven - Not sure. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The second thing is Disquiet. Disquiet really needs streamlining to remove bookkeeping, but in addition to that like to see it balanced so that you see a constant low level jerk behaviour to the Promethean rather than taking time to build up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now for some of the smaller things I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Alchemy and Mad Science rules. There's a lot of experimenting in the books, usually the Created themselves are experimenting on progeny. Lets have some rules for it. The fact that those rules can be reused for mortal NPCs is only a plus.<br /> <br /> More options for The Principle. Nearly every option given is some variant on preserving the status qou. <u>That is stupid!</u>. Firstly because it gives only one option, secondly because that one option doesn't fit the theme of the game. There should be at least one option for the Principle as The Pilgrimage on a cosmic scale.<br /> <br /> A book of &quot;quests&quot;. Prometheans spend a lot of their time moving away from things, usually disquiet and half formed wastlands. Lets have options for moving towards stuff. From low level stuff like seeing signs saying &quot;a big promethian meeting on this date and place&quot; and travelling to the convention to high level stuff like a tourist trip covering: The Garden of Eden, Osiris's kingdom in the Underworld, Frankenstine's original laboratory and the crater Satan made during his fall from heaven to hell. Or heck, an epic quest to save the world. The idea that hero's learn a lot about themselves on quests, famboy -&gt; jedi, is a popular one, and it fits in well with Promethean.<br /> <br /> Fix the rules for taking damage. IMO if you look at how Aggravated is handled it makes Promethians weaker than mortals. So here's my replacement. Promethians do not take any damage from Bashing or Lethal. Period. You can only hurt them with something that causes Aggravated Damage, or by doing so much damage that it wraps around, in that case inflict the Agg and ignore the rest. You can still inflict tilts though. The idea being that if you chop of it's leg, it's not exactly injured. There's no blood loss, there's no slow down, but it still can't walk on a missing leg.<br /> <br /> Introduce a golden rule: Every Promethian has a fair shot at the pilgrimage. You never have anything like an Extrepimor who can't create progeny. (Zeka and the like might still get into trouble afterwords, but becoming human is still clearly possible).<br /> <br /> Remove the need to create progeny. I've noticed a few people saying they feel the new dawn is bad / Promethean is not a hopeful game because of this. Anything that damages the themes that much must go; or possibly they're just outright wrong, but I kinda trust Jnsead's opinion.<br /> <br /> Humanity starts at 3. Promethians start with disadvantages that can get removed via milestones.<br /> <br /> Weird weird weird. This is a game about creation, and it's a game about people living outside of society. Those two things scream for weirdness. Stuff that dosn't fit into normal life. Just as a Promethian is always seeing new stuff for the first time, because they're probably like 3 years old, players should always be seeing new stuff to capture that feeling.<br /> <br /> Humour-seeming / Lineage-kith system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:27:13-08:00","id":3680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book#post3053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Humanity should be reworked to start at 3 and build up from there, with higher levels of Humanity making the Promethean <i>physically</i> more human as well as <i>mentally</i> more human.<br /> \u200b\u2022 Lineages should be generalized to Humours, with the existing Lineages being retained as customizations of Humours, much like how Kiths customize Seemings in <b>Changeling</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book#post3053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Athanors should be based on Refinements instead of Lineages.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought that once, now I think that Athanors should be free from any affinity.<br /> <br /> Refinement is how you become human, not what kind of human you want to become. Athanors are what kind of human you want to become.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book#post3053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Get rid of the ranking system for Transmutations. Handle them more like Embeds in <b>Demon</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could see this working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book#post3053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Revise Disquiet, preferably to interact with the Integrity of significant mortal characters (and with \u201cmook rules\u201d when dealing with characters who are individually unimportant). By default, assume that other supernaturals are immune to Disquiet, but give the Storyteller the option to have Disquiet interact with other supernaturals in their own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make Disquiet affect supernatural by default.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that what might be a good idea is to say that when you meet someone for the first time, roll disquiet to see if they treat you like jerks for a scene. Under special circumstances (like they saw your disfigurements, or a blatantly supernatural display) they roll to become a torch wielding mob vector for a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book#post3053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Revise Wasteland to streamline it, and to tie it more to use of Pyros in an area rather than merely the passage of time; address the question of if and how Wastelands recover as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO try to focus on reducing book keeping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don;t want a Qashmallim chronicle - I love those freaky angels, but 90% of the time (whether they're a messenger or harbinger of doom) they're walking, talking, burning plot device. They also have a lot of similarity with angels and demons, now. Them being reworked as a primary focus rather than a fringe weirdness would weaken Promethean, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Pandorans expanded and made a bit nastier - Dormacy should work a bit like the Weeping Angels, perhaps, and there should be ways for Pandorans to ijteract with humans and endure long periods of starvation without turning into stone - Prometheans are a <i>rare</i> food source. I have no idea how the Lady of Chains manages.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like nastier, but I'm not sold on them interacting with humans.<br /> <br /> I'd also quite like to remove any possibility that they regret what they are. I think it goes against the themes of Promethian is they can be stuck and unhappy because they hate being Pandorans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=3368#post3368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your Seeming/Kith idea... but I adore the Lineages. I really do. I think your 'kith' axis should be why the Promethean was made. because as it stands the Lineages are arguably more distinct by their intended purpose rather than their humour</div> </div> </div> </div> Point of order; it's how your progenitor was created <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You can of course try to use a new proecdure rather than repeat an old one but that's really dangerous. So in theory you could create a Plegmatic lover, but that's way harder than creating a Galataid.<br /> <br /> (BTW, Dataweaver. I'd let any Promethean create any possible Promethean. But they need a doner of the right Humour or some way of brewing up fresh humour in a lab)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:40:03-08:00","id":4015,"title":"","content":"Has it been confirmed in any way that Promethean will even get a Chronicle book? That would be amazing news if true!<br /> <br /> I would really like to see how Promethean scales with tiers. I think there is room for a look into what Promethean society could look like if it even coalesced out of the ether. I would also like to see a few more Lineages, even just as examples and not &quot;these exist&quot; and some refinements of the, errr, Refinements. Some of the ones introduced in Saturnine Nights seem especially in need of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:03:44-08:00","id":4034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=4015#post4015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been confirmed in any way that Promethean will even get a Chronicle book? That would be amazing news if true!</div> </div> </div> </div>It would, wouldn\u2019t it? But sadly, there\u2019s nothing but speculation right now; and barring a showing of interest in <b>Promethean</b> by the fans, there may never be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=4015#post4015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really like to see how Promethean scales with tiers. I think there is room for a look into what Promethean society could look like if it even coalesced out of the ether. I would also like to see a few more Lineages, even just as examples and not &quot;these exist&quot; and some refinements of the, errr, Refinements. Some of the ones introduced in Saturnine Nights seem especially in need of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>you mean <b>Magnum Opus</b>, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:12:04-08:00","id":4042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=4034#post4034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you mean <b>Magnum Opus</b>, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I do mean <b>Magnum Opus</b>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:13:14-08:00","id":4758,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4d change not a thing. This game is perfect to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T03:08:35-08:00","id":6709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b><br /> Humanity should be reworked to start at 3 and build up from there, with higher levels of Humanity making the Promethean physically more human as well as mentally more human. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about the physically more human part - I quite like how that's a point of sudden transformation - but otherwise, agreed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lineages should be generalized to Humours, with the existing Lineages being retained as customizations of Humours, much like how Kiths customize Seemings in Changeling. </div> </div> </div>I'm ambivalent about this, but I'd like it more if you'd said bloodline and clan - the story of the demiurge and progenitor is too important to write off as just a kith-analogue. Also, I seem to recall Blackhat_Matt said that he'd be the one doing this if it was done, and that he'd not want to change the Lineages. So anything we want here is probably a flight of fancy, although that I'd want would probably be more of one than this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Athanors should be based on Refinements instead of Lineages. </div> </div> </div>How do you see this meshing with the fact that Refinements are more likely to be changed than any other y-splat?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Include a box addressing if and how the Principle and its qashmallim differ from the God-Machine and its angels. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revise Disquiet, preferably to interact with the Integrity of significant mortal characters (and with \u201cmook rules\u201d when dealing with characters who are individually unimportant). </div> </div> </div>Agreed. A &quot;communal rule&quot; for dealing with masses of people at a time wouldn't hurt either.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Revise Wasteland to streamline it, and to tie it more to use of Pyros in an area rather than merely the passage of time; address the question of if and how Wastelands recover as well. </div> </div> </div>Certainly the Wasteland could do with being a bit clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Eremite:</b><br /> I don;t want a Qashmallim chronicle - I love those freaky angels, but 90% of the time (whether they're a messenger or harbinger of doom) they're walking, talking, burning plot device. </div> </div> </div>One of Blood and Smoke's developers (DaveB?) described the Strix Chronicle as about the clash between the suave vampires of pop-culture and the monstrous vampires of folklore, and those particularly bad cases where it's <i>not</i> a clash. The God Machine Chronicle is about the grind of a purpose you may or may not be part of (I'd suggest praying you're not, but if you did it might hear you).<br /> <br /> Those present a sort of default of what chronicles are about. But the default for Promethean is the Pilgrimmage - without that, it's not really Promethean any more. So I agree with you about a Qashmalim Chronicle - and extend the same sentiment to a Mad Science Chronicle, Zeka Chronicle, or Sublimatus Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Mortals is the only possibility that gets round that.<br /> <br /> But what I really think is that the Promethean book should be, in comparison to the others, scattershot. Promethean is suited to an episodic style, as the Created move around a lot, and move from milestone to milestone - and so I think the Tales should be about as many different things as possible - things that an ST can adapt into personal milestones to further personal Pilgrimmages. Rather than tiers as such, move out from the throng to the wider world: five tales focussed on other Prometheans or the environment, five tales focussed on human interactions with Prometheans, five tales focussed on human interactions with other humans, and five tales focussed on the wider mythos (a Qashmal's mission gone awry, a devastating Firestorm threatening Prometheans and humans alike, the machinations of a Sublimatus, the Unfleshed...).<br /> <br /> <br /> Stuff I'd want:<br /> <br /> The Bronze and Lead Refinements in the new core. I'm less fussed about the other two, though they'd be cool as well, but study of the flesh and forging a communal bond have a particular spice.<br /> <br /> I mentioned flights of fancy, above. One thing I'd like is for the Ulgan to be replaced with something based on the &quot;Underworldly oracles&quot; of myth. If we must have a Lineage crossing with an otherworld, I think the ghostly is better than Shadow spirits. Also, I think many of the motifs that attend mythical oracles work well for Promethean - the unkind truth, the obscure truth, the hostility and doubt shown to those whose visions aren't what the client wants, mad ecstasies.<br /> <br /> Some new corebook inclusion of Constructs and Extemporae (the former in with the Lineages, the latter perhaps in a Tale).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 11-09-2013, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T03:40:40-08:00","id":6718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm ambivalent about this, but I'd like it more if you'd said bloodline and clan - the story of the demiurge and progenitor is too important to write off as just a kith-analogue. Also, I seem to recall Blackhat_Matt said that he'd be the one doing this if it was done, and that he'd not want to change the Lineages. So anything we want here is probably a flight of fancy, although that I'd want would probably be more of one than this.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason the &quot;Kith&quot; analogue can't have full splat sized write ups, like they do now.<br /> <br /> If you look at the books, it's <u>obvious</u> that the later writers gave up on the 5-splat thing. Even if you think of Zeka as an antagonist splat (which they're clearly not) you have loads of rules for new Lineages that are not lineages. Constructs, Extempores, mentions of minor lineages here and there, Unfleshed; Unfleshed are basically generic Lineage creation rules.<br /> <br /> So why not present 5 core Lienages; but say from the start that there's more than just the 5 (perhaps none are as large as the core 5) and design the rules from the start on the assumption that yes, players will be playing non-core Lineages. Where it matters mechanically, such as Branded Throngs, the rules should be built to accommodate non-core Lineages. Saying that Humour, not Lineage, is the important part preserves the rules as intended across an infinite number of Lineages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned flights of fancy, above. One thing I'd like is for the Ulgan to be replaced with something based on the &quot;Underworldly oracles&quot; of myth. If we must have a Lineage crossing with an otherworld, I think the ghostly is better than Shadow spirits. Also, I think many of the motifs that attend mythical oracles work well for Promethean - the unkind truth, the obscure truth, the hostility and doubt shown to those whose visions aren't what the client wants, mad ecstasies.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's actually a pretty good idea. Strange Alchemies already presents the possibility that Orpheus was a Progenitor (I'm not sure if the myth ever has him being put back together though)<br /> <br /> Alternatively Zombis where a person is ritually poisioned and burried alive only to rise again as a Promethian.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:37:16-08:00","id":6752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you see this meshing with the fact that Refinements are more likely to be changed than any other y-splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever Refinement you have when you decide to take on an Athanor is the one that decides the availability of Athanors.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. A &quot;communal rule&quot; for dealing with masses of people at a time wouldn't hurt either.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an extension of the \u201cmook rules\u201d: when you\u2019re dealing with mobs, you\u2019re not dealing with individuals; so with a few notable exceptions (e.g., the ringleader), everyone in the mob is almost by definition an Extra.<br /> <br /> One of Blood and Smoke's developers (DaveB?) described the Strix Chronicle as about the clash between the suave vampires of pop-culture and the monstrous vampires of folklore, and those particularly bad cases where it's <i>not</i> a clash. The God Machine Chronicle is about the grind of a purpose you may or may not be part of (I'd suggest praying you're not, but if you did it might hear you).<br /> <br /> Those present a sort of default of what chronicles are about. But the default for Promethean is the Pilgrimage \u2014 without that, it's not really Promethean any more. So I agree with you about a Qashmallim Chronicle \u2014 and extend the same sentiment to a Mad Science Chronicle, Zeka Chronicle, or Sublimatus Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Mortals is the only possibility that gets round that.[/QUOTE]Exactly. From the get-go, the thing that has most made <b>Promethean</b> different from every other line has been its focus on humanity. Even <b>Hunter</b>, where the protagonists <i>are</i> humans, is more about the monsters they fight than it is about humans. By having the goal of the Pilgrimage be to become human, and the method of the Pilgrimage be to learn about human nature, <b>Promethean</b> places regular humans in the spotlight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff I'd want:<br /> <br /> The Bronze and Lead Refinements in the new core. I'm less fussed about the other two, though they'd be cool as well, but study of the flesh and forging a communal bond have a particular spice.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Strange Alchemies</b> had a set of communal Transmutations that every Promethean had an Affinity for. I\u2019d either roll those into the Bronze Refinement\u2019s specialty Transmutations or I\u2019d fold the latter into the former and ditch the Bronze Refinement as a separate thing. More generally though, I\u2019d like the core book to provide the seven Refinements that correspond to the seven alchemical metals (that is, the core five plus Silver and Lead). Granted, Silver is in the odd position of being designed largely to facilitate crossovers; but I could see refocusing it primarily on ephemeral beings and secondarily on whatever other oddities inhabit the World of Darkness, with the likes of vampires, werewolves, mages, etc. being downplayed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=6709#post6709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned flights of fancy, above. One thing I'd like is for the Ulgan to be replaced with something based on the &quot;Underworldly oracles&quot; of myth. If we must have a Lineage crossing with an otherworld, I think the ghostly is better than Shadow spirits. Also, I think many of the motifs that attend mythical oracles work well for Promethean - the unkind truth, the obscure truth, the hostility and doubt shown to those whose visions aren't what the client wants, mad ecstasies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one reason why I\u2019d rather put the primary focus on the Humours rather than the Lineages: Ulgans and Orpheans are both of the Ectoplasmic Humour; they just manifest it differently. I get what you mean about the difference between \u201cKith\u201d vs. \u201cBloodline\u201d; and for the record, I was thinking of something closer to the latter than the former. The main difference in my perspective, and the reason why I spoke in terms of Kiths rather than Bloodlines, is that a Bloodline is something that you might acquire sometime later in your career, if you choose to pursue it; a Kith is something that you start out with, unless you specifically ask not to have one. Lineages would be even less optional than Kiths are, and would add flesh to the Humours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:43:16-08:00","id":6911,"title":"","content":"Maybe re-designing the rules on &quot;Wastelands&quot;. Making them easier to create/calculate/sum up the effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:09:31-08:00","id":6933,"title":"","content":"All I want is for the book to play Oingo Boingo's &quot;Weird Science&quot; whenever I open it, like a cheap birthday card.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:15:55-08:00","id":7207,"title":"","content":"Simplified Wasteland, Disquiet, and Torment rules.<br /> <br /> I think Dataweaver's right in that the linchpin of the Chronicle should be mortals, but I also think that if you're running Promethean and mortals <i>aren't </i>your leading and most dangerous antagonists, then you're avoiding the heart of the game. That said, a reboot that keeps that front and center and updates the system is what I want. Promethean is one of two games I'd likely give to a KS for (Wraith being the other, hell yes!), but not if it threatened to radically undermine what makes it so swell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:02:51-08:00","id":9611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Verge:</b>I think Dataweaver's right in that the linchpin of the Chronicle should be mortals, but I also think that if you're running Promethean and mortals aren't your leading and most dangerous antagonists, then you're avoiding the heart of the game. </div> </div> </div>Mortals and the Pilgrimmage. But it can't be about the Pilgrimmage per se, because it's too personal to each individual Promethean - that's why I suggested making it scattershot earlier, so as to give a wide palatte to incorporate into milestones.<br /> <br /> But to combine scattershot and mortals... well, when it comes to making Prometheans, human obsession is the coin of the realm. Perhaps the same is true of other manifestations of the Fire. The Qashmalim seem to be drivers of events, and they certainly manipulate - but perhaps their actions are in answer to a driving obsession - someone wants something badly enough, and Qashmalim are answering that &quot;prayer.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, people sufficiently burned out and apathetic five succor to the Flux, not the Azoth - crush enough feeling out of people, and they're hardly there. Maybe they don't cause Dormancy like other people, and their faded communities become havens for Pandorans.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, fury - in the sense of tempestuous feeling rather than anger - could be mirrored in Firestorms.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness has several otherworlds that react to the psyche of those who move through them, but in Gothic literature and classic horror films - which Promethean takes a lot of its feel from - the natural world's rather like that too, if the emotions are extreme enough. (I think the term's &quot;pathetic fallacy&quot;). So that's what the Fire does - it answers the heart, in more ways than just making Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Not all the time, of course: it has to be extreme, just like it does when a Promethean is made. But maybe the Wasteland makes it easier - rather than turning the world to muck, it seeds it with Fire that then starts to answer the hidden prayers in people's hearts with Storms and Angels. Furious obsession is the coin of the realm, and Prometheans carry that realm around with them.<br /> <br /> And that makes the Wasteland double-edged. Most Prometheans want to understand humans, and a Wasteland effect that writes humanity's foibles onto the landscape is one they might believe - rightly or wrongly - will help them do so. They have a reason to stay and let it develop (though of course hidden obsessions being nurtured into that kind of violent expression is also hella destructive, which ties back into Disquiet and torch-wielding mobs).<br /> <br /> Ok, that turned into a bit of a stream. Hope it makes sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T09:30:01-08:00","id":49045,"title":"","content":"I agree wholeheartedly with changing Disquiet and Wasteland to shore up bookkeeping. <br /> <br /> I had a thought regarding Disquiet that I think would work well(ish) with the new rules: Disquiet as Integrity modifier. Basically, if a Mortal were to ever glimpse a Promethean's true nature (or, perhaps, if they fail a Resolve+Composure roll), they receive a Breaking Point along the lines of the Prommie's Disquiet effect (<i>not</i> becoming obsessed with a Galatean, for example). Factors such as Azoth and having, er, Tormented that scene (among others, I'm sure) would make the Breaking Point even harder to ignore. For Supernatural Beings, these factors would determine <i>were</i> along Humanity/Harmony/Whatever the Breaking Point would sit (more negatives garnered, the lower on the chart it sits). Perhaps this effect could become a permanent thing should the Disquieted being be affected by it enough times.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I felt that this would be a cool way of handling it (without simply resorting to Condition effects), though I can't say how this would mess up the other systems. <br /> <br /> As per the &quot;plot&quot; behind the book, I think it should be the &quot;Created Chronicles&quot; and should focus on Creation vs. Creator, the founding of purpose within &quot;ourselves&quot; and in others, ties that bind, and the things that drive Prometheans forward. I'd like to see the Qashmallim pushed &quot;back&quot; a bit, made more of a mysterious <i>event</i> than simply a new spirit type. I'd like to see rules for Mortals utilizing Azoth and Flux for alchemy and weird science (and the resulting backlash that comes from such levels of maddening obsession and the utilization of forces beyond one's understanding). I'd like to see the focus less on &quot;meta-purpose&quot; (i.e. The Principle) and more on filling out a Promethean's personal mission. I'd also like to see Pandorans (and in some ways Centimani) seen more as &quot;failures&quot; of the Great Work, dead ends along the path to Humanity, than &quot;bad guys filled with <i>evil</i> magic&quot; (I'm not saying that's what they are at all, it's just the impression I get from reading the books). <br /> <br /> I'd also like to see rules and examples in this book for Prometheans <i>building</i> something of a Society, perhaps due to the PCs involvement. I think it'd be interesting to have some sort of Crunch for building up a brand new Supernatural society from Tier 1 to Tier 3 (or maybe even beyond... <i>sidebar!</i>), with rules and effects for joining various PC/ST created groups as well as having an idea regarding how much bullshit would potentially be involved in such an endevour. <br /> <br /> Love, Peace, and Chicken Grease,<br /> The Mighty Grendel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1931-the-mighty-grendel","name":"The Mighty Grendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1931_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T23:52:52-08:00","id":49595,"title":"","content":"Minor idea: the Refinement of Lead in the revised core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T07:18:29-08:00","id":49763,"title":"","content":"It is a small thing, but I feel like the rules for resurrection, including the Revivification Bestowment, should be re-examined &amp; revised. Something about the way it currently works feels...off. I never fully grasped why one could only come back to life once. I could see a system in which every time you come back, you lose something in the process (Azoth resetting to 1, yes, but perhaps other things too. Transmutations. Humanity.). Perhaps there is a choice to be made, whether to resurrect or give up on the Pilgrimage and stay dead for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:37:26-08:00","id":50088,"title":"","content":"The thing that I want is to make a Promethean's progress on the pilgrimage a little easier to track for the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T18:01:05-08:00","id":51241,"title":"","content":"So now we know that Blood and Smoke has a very different structure from God Machine chronicles... and one that I think is better suited to Promethean. In light of which - and with the benefit of some time - I'm revisiting some of my (and others') earlier comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b><br /> Given the game's focus on learning about humanity and striving to achieve Mortality, I think the default plot drivers should be humans: e.g., The Long Journey: the Mortal Chronicle. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the <i>word</i> &quot;mortal&quot; quite works, but I still strongly agree with the sentiment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bLineages should be generalized to Humours, with the existing Lineages being retained as customizations of Humours, much like how Kiths customize Seemings in Changeling. </div> </div> </div>I still don't care for this, unless the modification is much greater than for kiths. If mortals should be the touchstone, then the mortal obsession that drove a demiurge, and its ability to indelibly mark the resulting Lineage, should be a big deal. I <i>could</i> maybe get behind something like this:<br /> <br /> Humour: Determines the form of the Wasteland (and implications if the Promethean joins a Pact), and governs favoured access to one set of Transmutations.*<br /> <br /> Lineage: Is where the origin story comes in. Determines Disfigurements, Disquiet, and Torment. In setting terms, the latter two parallel the demiurge's obsessions, and determine which Humour becomes dominant in a given Lineage (out of setting, it's presumably more likely to be the other way round).<br /> <br /> * Assuming the same Lineages, Refinements, and Transmutations: Alchemicus would go to Phelegmatic Prometheans,** Electrification to Choleric ones, Mesmerism to Sanguine ones, Sensorium to Ectoplasmic ones, and Vitality to Melancholic ones.<br /> <br /> ** No, Alchemicus isn't a great fit for the Osirians, but it is a good fit for a phlegmatic bent.<br /> <br /> Under this model, Refinements would grant favoured access to one set of Transmutations rather than one (their remaining one for the main five, their unique one for the supplemental four, and Irradiation for Centimani).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Athanors should be based on Refinements instead of Lineages. </div> </div> </div>I'm on board with this now. Athanors are about aspirations for the future, and that fits Refinements better than Lineage. I'd throw in a rule that once you've picked an Athanor, the &quot;swapping into this Refinement is quicker and out of it slower than normal&quot; rule applies to the one corresponding to your Athanor rather than necessarily Stannum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>TheKingsRaven:</b><br /> Alchemy and Mad Science rules. There's a lot of experimenting in the books, usually the Created themselves are experimenting on progeny. Lets have some rules for it. </div> </div> </div>In this case, I would keep it simple, and allow humans a way of gaining access to Transmutations if they're off-the-rails enough. None of &quot;spiritual purification&quot; stuff though - that's for Prometheans - humans who mess with this are broken and break themselves further doing it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So here's my replacement. Promethians do not take any damage from Bashing or Lethal. Period. You can only hurt them with something that causes Aggravated Damage, or by doing so much damage that it wraps around, in that case inflict the Agg and ignore the rest. </div> </div> </div>I think that's excessive, though I could get behind an &quot;all nominally lethal damage is actually bashing&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Me:</b><br /> Also, I seem to recall Blackhat_Matt said that he'd be the one doing this if it was done, and that he'd not want to change the Lineages. So anything we want here is probably a flight of fancy ... [like] ... the Ulgan to be replaced with something based on the &quot;Underworldly oracles&quot; of myth. If we must have a Lineage crossing with an otherworld, I think the ghostly is better than Shadow spirits. Also, I think many of the motifs that attend mythical oracles work well for Promethean - the unkind truth, the obscure truth, the hostility and doubt shown to those whose visions aren't what the client wants, mad ecstasies. </div> </div> </div>If there were to be a Humour/Lineage division, then I'd be on board with adding a second Lineage for each Humour, and making the second Lineage something off the norm; for example:<br /> <br /> Choleric: Maybe an Unfleshed Lineage, though I don't have any more specific idea than that.<br /> <br /> Sanguine: Maybe a supernatural Lineage, like if that vampire-made Promethean from Saturnine Night managed to make more of his kind.<br /> <br /> Phegmatic: An Lineage whose founder was an Extemporae from a serious natural disaster.<br /> <br /> Melancholic: Both the Osirians and Tammuz have the attempted resurrection of a loved one in their origin, but neither of them reflect the loss/grief vibe. I would suggest replacing the canon Tammuz with a group that do, and put the slave vibe into a Lineage of actual golems (as in Constructs).<br /> <br /> Ectoplasmic: My oracle idea, with the explicit myth that the demiurge and progenitor are one and the same; ie, that she called the fire down into her own flesh and made herself something new.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what I really think is that the Promethean book should be, in comparison to the others, scattershot. Promethean is suited to an episodic style, as the Created move around a lot, and move from milestone to milestone - and so I think the Tales should be about as many different things as possible - things that an ST can adapt into personal milestones to further personal Pilgrimmages. </div> </div> </div>I wrote this when I assumed that any Chronicle book would follow the general structure of God Machine Chronicles. Since we now know that's not the case, I abandon it as a suggestion (especially since I don't think Tales are a very good fit for Promethean).<br /> <br /> What I'd rather have is a breakdown something like in Blood and Smoke:<br /> <br /> Who You Are (I think the second person fits Promethean better): Covers the Lineages, Humours if they're separate, and Refinements.<br /> <br /> The Long Road: Covers the general myths, and what little society they've managed to scape together. And the general structure of a Pilgrimmage.<br /> <br /> Clay and Lead: Character creation, Transmutations, generally how Promethan bodies work, that sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> The Burning World: Covers manifestations of the Fire. Pandorans, Qashmalim, Firestorms, the Wasteland, whatever rules there are for letting mortals gain access to Transmutations.<br /> <br /> No Rest: A variety of mortal templates (including a simplified Integrity system to go with Disquiet); and some specific sample people. The Disquiet (and maybe Torment) rules. And advice for/samples of: roadside stops like motels, diners and campgrounds; small towns; slightly larger towns; and city environments; together with the fracture lines in each that Disquiet can aggravate [I'm thinking in terms of chapter 1 of Midnight Roads here; short and numerous rather than few and detailed].<br /> <br /> [Putting the Disquiet and Torment here was deliberate - essentially, the rules for interacting with humans going with the rules for the humans themselves]<br /> <br /> And rule and storytelling chapters of course.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T08:48:57-08:00","id":51641,"title":"","content":"Personally, were it I, I would change the Ulgan to the Lazarean - these are the dead brought back by beseeching a higher power, as a sign of faith and devotion. Due to the <b>Supine</b> imbalance they constantly seek the approval and love of others (or a higher being) even unto self destruction. Kind of the anti-Osiran,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T13:23:33-08:00","id":51821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>could</i> maybe get behind something like this:<br /> <br /> Humour: Determines the form of the Wasteland (and implications if the Promethean joins a Pact), and governs favoured access to one set of Transmutations.*<br /> <br /> Lineage: Is where the origin story comes in. Determines Disfigurements, Disquiet, and Torment. In setting terms, the latter two parallel the demiurge's obsessions, and determine which Humour becomes dominant in a given Lineage (out of setting, it's presumably more likely to be the other way round).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part that's how I always envisioned it. Have a look at my old notes on the Gods Domain wiki.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under this model, Refinements would grant favoured access to one set of Transmutations rather than one (their remaining one for the main five, their unique one for the supplemental four, and Irradiation for Centimani).</div> </div> </div> </div>I preferred it as them having two and you swap one out; basically how Zeka work now but for everyone. The reason comes down to the Flux Refinements. I imagined three of them:<ul><li>If the world treats me as a monster then I'll be a monster.</li> <li>You know, being a Promethian isn't that bad. I'll say like this.</li> <li>Humans are weak, I'll go on a different pilgramage to become superhuman instead.</li> </ul><br /> For the middle one in particular, Pandoran Transmutations aren't that fitting. So I thought that if they had Pandoran + other, you could swap out Pandoran.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, I would keep it simple, and allow humans a way of gaining access to Transmutations if they're off-the-rails enough. None of &quot;spiritual purification&quot; stuff though - that's for Prometheans - humans who mess with this are broken and break themselves further doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div> No. That's silly. Alchemy has always been about spiritual purification. What's the point of basing a game on Alchemy and saying that it's core tenant was completely delusional. Or all the mortal Alchemists you meet are broken and decaying for their practices (rather than the one cannon alchemist mortal NPC who's what, Morality 8? 9?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's excessive, though I could get behind an &quot;all nominally lethal damage is actually bashing&quot; rule.</div> </div> </div> </div> Being excessive was the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Choleric: Maybe an Unfleshed Lineage, though I don't have any more specific idea than that.</div> </div> </div> </div> After one unkowing Demiurge spent years obsessively posting on Facebook (or similar) under a fake persona a server transformed into an Unfleshed and wondered off, convinced that it was said fake persona. However said fake was actually a pretty badly written one. More a collection of stereotypes than a plausible person. As a result the resulting lineage has Choleric passion and drive but no substance to direct it; instead they latch onto external ideologies or cultural groups and direct their energy though them, probably making any real member of the group cringe at the loud aggressive, ignorant walking stereotype.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, playing this lineage is about discovering that you're a person not just a collection of labels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phegmatic: An Lineage whose founder was an Extemporae from a serious natural disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div> A man cryogenically frozen came back when a pyros charged lightning bolt hit the power line for his pod. They are noted for exceptionally good memories of their former lives - nearly all believe they are the same person - and have to struggle really hard to develop as a person rather than remain mostly the same for eternity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51241#post51241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Melancholic: Both the Osirians and Tammuz have the attempted resurrection of a loved one in their origin, but neither of them reflect the loss/grief vibe. I would suggest replacing the canon Tammuz with a group that do, and put the slave vibe into a Lineage of actual golems (as in Constructs).</div> </div> </div> </div> I approve; coincidently I think that the Construct/Unflehsed division is unnecessary. I'd just give each Lineage a material that they're made from (all Golems are clay) and mechanics to reflect that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51641#post51641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, were it I, I would change the Ulgan to the Lazarean - these are the dead brought back by beseeching a higher power, as a sign of faith and devotion. Due to the <b>Supine</b> imbalance they constantly seek the approval and love of others (or a higher being) even unto self destruction. Kind of the anti-Osiran,</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeking approval and love sounds a little too similar to the Galataids to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T14:50:05-08:00","id":51897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=4015#post4015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been confirmed in any way that Promethean will even get a Chronicle book? That would be amazing news if true!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not confirmed, but in an AMA, somebody (maybe Rich) commented that they'd love to do it if GMC/B&amp;S/Etc do well. I think they threw the name &quot;Qashmallim Chronicles&quot; out there, but that might have just been to use as some kind of place-holder and not an actual indication of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T14:53:33-08:00","id":51904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51821#post51821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. That's silly. Alchemy has always been about spiritual purification. What's the point of basing a game on Alchemy and saying that it's core tenant was completely delusional. Or all the mortal Alchemists you meet are broken and decaying for their practices (rather than the one cannon alchemist mortal NPC who's what, Morality 8? 9?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as often as you might think, no. But if you want spiritual perfection, adapt the Pilgrimmage - but first they must break. (Mostly though, my comment was about wanting to keep them second tier).<br /> <br /> I like the facebook Lineage idea; they also partake of the Dreamborn, and an <i>accidental</i> demiurge is new element.<br /> <br /> I'm less keen on the cryogenic Lineage. It's not a bad idea, but I think it should be something more primal; Hurricane Katrina or the Asian Tsunami were what I had in mind when I suggested it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T15:17:50-08:00","id":51928,"title":"","content":"By \u201csecond-tier\u201d, I assume you\u2019re meaning \u201cnot as important to the game as Prometheans\u201d (as opposed to \u201coperate in a regional, not local or global, scope\u201d)? I\u2019d agree with that, although the distnction should be one of page-count and how the issue is framed rather than what is or isn\u2019t possible: if you want to play a mortal who seeks an alchemical goal of perfection, <b>Mortal Chronicle</b> shouldn\u2019t say \u201cthou shalt not\u201d. At the most, it should hint at the possibility but justify not giving \u201cmortal Pilgrimage\u201d rules in the core book by saying \u201cthis book is about Prometheans\u201d. But a <i>God\u2019s Domain</i>-style supplement that focuses on mortals who have been touched by the Divine Fire (roughly analogous to ghouls or Proximi)? Sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T15:50:01-08:00","id":51944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51904#post51904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not as often as you might think, no. But if you want spiritual perfection, adapt the Pilgrimmage - but first they must break. (Mostly though, my comment was about wanting to keep them second tier).</div> </div> </div> </div> Making them second tier like Ghouls is fine, this does not require breaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51904#post51904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm less keen on the cryogenic Lineage. It's not a bad idea, but I think it should be something more primal; Hurricane Katrina or the Asian Tsunami were what I had in mind when I suggested it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal and Plegmatic seems like an odd combination. My suggestion would be to start with an idea of what's broken or missing (actually for Plegmatic I'd definitely say what's missing) and must be fixed during the pilgrimage. Then work backwards towards an origin story.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you like the Facebook idea, stereotype to real person just seems so right for Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51928#post51928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the most, it should hint at the possibility but justify not giving \u201cmortal Pilgrimage\u201d rules in the core book by saying \u201cthis book is about Prometheans\u201d. But a <i>God\u2019s Domain</i>-style supplement that focuses on mortals who have been touched by the Divine Fire (roughly analogous to ghouls or Proximi)? Sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say a Ghoul style appendix is best. A bit of backround about how/why you become an Alchemist (read books, learn from teachers), personalties that are drawn to or emerge from Alchemy (mostly, as in what happens to your personality if you spend all day in a lab), and any rules changes that must be taken into account if you're a mortal rather than a Promethean.<br /> <br /> If there's space you can present rules for achieving Enlightenment, if not that can be presented as a bit of fluff to be expanded in another book (The Blood Sorceries equivalent) or even a Hunter book. I mean, there is that giant Conspiracy of Alchemists, surely some of them try for the gold; and the inevitable cannon or fannon Rabbi Conspiracy should have their own equivalent to enhance the thematic parallels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T05:08:38-08:00","id":53129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=51821#post51821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeking approval and love sounds a little too similar to the Galataids to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's more like... Justification, then? They want to know that what their doing is the right thing, that it's not all in vain. It's Supine to the Sanguine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:24:58-08:00","id":56323,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Disquiet might affect other supernaturals differently.<br /> <br /> Developers have said they're looking for analogies in each post-GMC splat for the new Vampire predatory aura, which affects how Vampires interact with each other but in B&amp;S it's also hinted it affects other supernaturals in their own unique ways as well. It's been stated that there'll be something of the sort in the Idigam Chronicles, as well as re-working a Mage's nimbus into something somewhat similar, too.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Disquiet can act like Promethean's analogy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:21:47-08:00","id":56360,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, there are two main differences between Predatory Aura and Disquiet (as it currently is): first, Predatory Aura affects <i>everyone</i>; Disquiet doesn\u2019t affect other Prometheans. Second, Predatory Aura is a tool that the vampire can bring to bear, which sometimes gets out of control; Disquiet\u2026 not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:45:08-08:00","id":56394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=56360#post56360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, there are two main differences between Predatory Aura and Disquiet (as it currently is): first, Predatory Aura affects <i>everyone</i>; Disquiet doesn\u2019t affect other Prometheans. Second, Predatory Aura is a tool that the vampire can bring to bear, which sometimes gets out of control; Disquiet\u2026 not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is Disquietism, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T05:01:41-08:00","id":56662,"title":"","content":"Well, developers stated they would be rough analogies, not exactly perfect replicas. There's nothing wrong with having an exception now and then, either, in saying that Disquiet wouldn't affect other Prometheans. These mechanics seem to have in common theme an idea of <i>social interaction</i>, and that's what Disquiet is.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm saying that it seems most people don't like, for any number of reasons, how Disquiet currently works. We also know that they'd be looking for that <i>social </i><i>interaction</i> mechanic in regards to Promethean. While it's possible to build something new, it's still kinda obvious that it'd be better to rework what's currently around. That's what most of Blood &amp; Smoke is, after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:32:15-08:00","id":56897,"title":"","content":"This is admittedly based only on reading the book after getting it from Drive Thru RPG when it was free... but I'd like to see more options for mortal-created Prometheans. I was a bit disappointed to find out that there's only one mortal Demiurge for every Lineage. I think that mad, desperate mortals creating Prometheans has a lot of potential and that restricting the propagation of the &quot;species&quot; to Prometheans creating more of their own ends in a loss of opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:48:30-08:00","id":56908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=56897#post56897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is admittedly based only on reading the book after getting it from Drive Thru RPG when it was free... but I'd like to see more options for mortal-created Prometheans. I was a bit disappointed to find out that there's only one mortal Demiurge for every Lineage. I think that mad, desperate mortals creating Prometheans has a lot of potential and that restricting the propagation of the &quot;species&quot; to Prometheans creating more of their own ends in a loss of opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually a thing. Admittedly the rarity of disseminated instructions for creation rituals other than Frankenstein's throws off the proportions, but multiple mortal demiurges exist for all the Lineages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T13:12:15-08:00","id":58272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b><br /> By \u201csecond-tier\u201d, I assume you\u2019re meaning \u201cnot as important to the game as Prometheans\u201d (as opposed to \u201coperate in a regional, not local or global, scope\u201d)? </div> </div> </div>Correct.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d agree with that, although the distnction should be one of page-count and how the issue is framed rather than what is or isn\u2019t possible: if you want to play a mortal who seeks an alchemical goal of perfection, Mortal Chronicle shouldn\u2019t say \u201cthou shalt not\u201d </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I guess. But in that case, I would go with the same keep it simple principle that led me to suggest that mortal alchemy rules should be rendered by giving humans a way to get access to Transmutations, and simply say that they can undertake a version of the Pilgrimmage.<br /> <br /> Incidentally the idea of this being a <i>Mortal</i> Chronicle was why I suggested the alchemists should be broken: the &quot;mortal&quot; it's talking about is the kind that fuels the day-to-day world; it's that that Prometheans have to get their own mortality from. Humans who go looking for Fire and bury themselves in the world of the Prometheans... well, it's fitting that the opposite happens and they burn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>TheKingsRaven:</b><br /> Making them second tier like Ghouls is fine, this does not require breaking. </div> </div> </div>It's &quot;What is to be united by Azoth must first be broken apart&quot; that requires breaking. Just as a &quot;donor's&quot; body must be torn apart before it can be remade into a Promethean, and a demiurge must be gripped by an obsession that stretches further than the world can accommodate, any mortal alchemist must be broken before the Fire will answer them. If you want them to have a Pilgrimmage available, I conceded that in my reply to Dataweaver, but making them unbroken in the first place goes against what the Fire's manifestations do people the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primal and Plegmatic seems like an odd combination. </div> </div> </div>But primal and <i>Water</i>, the element behind the Humour, do not.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My suggestion would be to start with an idea of what's broken or missing (actually for Plegmatic I'd definitely say what's missing) </div> </div> </div>In the case of Extemporae, what's missing is any connection to humanity at all - even more than most Prometheans, who at least have a human's motives lying behind the origin of tbeir Lineage. From that, I would picture their Lineage traits revolvong around the pitiless - not in the sense of malignity, but in the sense of them being forces made flesh. We fear them like we fear storms rather than monsters, except this storm's a monster as well. Water's a good fit for that; and the implacable drive side of Phlegm isn't bad either.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then work backwards towards an origin story. </div> </div> </div>Water's also a good source of natural disasters on a fittingly large scale for Extemporae, while hurricanes mix the power of air, and by secondary effects earth and fire, into the area of effect as well. It's not like thinking it through hadn't occurred to me when I first posted it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [b]reseru:<br /> I guess I'm saying that it seems most people don't like, for any number of reasons, how Disquiet currently works. We also know that they'd be looking for that social interaction mechanic in regards to Promethean. </div> </div> </div>Modifying Disquiet's mechanics to function more like Predatory aura - and, say, giving each Lineage a &quot;signature adjective&quot; for its Disquiet, and signature Condition it inflicts, in analogy to the different aspects of the Beast - is certainly worth exploring. But it should still be a burden to the Promethean, not something she can use.<br /> <br /> It also seems like an approach that would be easy to make mook and group versions of, for interactions with bit part NPC's and/or crowds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T15:38:09-08:00","id":58365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=58272#post58272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with the same keep it simple principle that led me to suggest that mortal alchemy rules should be rendered by giving humans a way to get access to Transmutations, and simply say that they can undertake a version of the Pilgrimmage.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd rather give Promethians free-form blood sorcery style Alchemy and give mortal alchemists access to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=58272#post58272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally the idea of this being a <i>Mortal</i> Chronicle was why I suggested the alchemists should be broken: the &quot;mortal&quot; it's talking about is the kind that fuels the day-to-day world; it's that that Prometheans have to get their own mortality from. Humans who go looking for Fire and bury themselves in the world of the Prometheans... well, it's fitting that the opposite happens and they burn.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really.<br /> <br /> The whole point of fire is that if it's not treated with respect it will burn you, but if it's treated with respect and care it is the most useful tool mankind ever had.<br /> <br /> Frankenstine tampered in God's Domain and was punished for his hubris. Judah Loew was a Rabbi and knew how to handle God's power with respect and so he got a loyal servant until he neglected his divine obligations and forgot to deactivate the Golem for the Sabbath (at least that's one version of the story).<br /> <br /> I think that both these variants have a place in Promethean. In the nWoD age-metaphor Promethian is Childhood, relationships with the creator (or their intellectual heirs, etc) is important. Hence it's vital that there's more than one type of in-the-know mortal to interact with than just the broken madmen (of science).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=58272#post58272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's &quot;What is to be united by Azoth must first be broken apart&quot; that requires breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div> Firstly, who says the Alchemist is trying to unite themselves? Sure some will be but others wont.<br /> <br /> Secondly, if you look at Alchemical theory it's not breaking apart. It's dissolving. That's a controlled process designed specifically to lead to reforging. It's not madness and internal collapse. It's spiritual purification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=58272#post58272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But primal and <i>Water</i>, the element behind the Humour, do not.In the case of Extemporae, what's missing is any connection to humanity at all</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't see that working as a lineage. There's no &quot;core flaw&quot;, thematically it's too broad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:31:36-08:00","id":67183,"title":"","content":"Electrification Transmutations for pre-electric eras. Possibly a non-technological source of healing as well, such as alchemical elixirs. <br /> <br /> Possibly extinct, alternate lineages for each of the &quot;five&quot; humours. Alternate takes or necessities of the Generative Act (why would any lineage ever branch, given the costs and abomination of creating another Promethean).<br /> <br /> A much better layout for Pandoran rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T15:54:53-08:00","id":67455,"title":"","content":"On the first two, I\u2019m hoping that the Promethean Dark Era will be far enough back in time to justify both \u2014 at least in part. If it\u2019s set prior to the 19th century, it will predate both electricity as a technology and Frankenstein: the former would all but require an overhaul of the Electrification Transmutations, and the latter would require addressing the lack of the Wretched Lineage. <br /> <br /> More generally though, I agree about having something of a split between Lineage and Humour. Drawing a loose analogy to Vampire, I like to think of Humours as being like Clans: broad, general archetypes of the different sorts of Prometheans that exist; whereas Lineages should be a bit more like Bloodlines: specialized cases of the general archetypes that the Humours represent. The main difference would be that Lineages would be mandatory (like Changeling\u2019s Kiths) rather than optional (like Vampire\u2019s Bloodlines). Put another way, Humours would have a timeless quality to them \u2014 you should get the sense that the five Humours have been around as long as Prometheans have existed, and may in fact reflect innate qualities of the Divine Fire itself \u2014 whereas Lineages are something with distinct lifespans: you can point to the first Frankenstein monster, and if the last Promethean in a Lineage dies before creating progeny, the Lineage itself dies. The last Frankenstein won\u2019t be the last Choleric; but the next Choleric will be created using a different generative act and will manifest the Choleric Humour in a different way than the Frankensteins did. (Unless someone rediscovers Frankenstein\u2019s notes and replicates his feat closely enough to resurrect the Frankenstein Lineage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T18:50:08-08:00","id":67561,"title":"","content":"Okay. Now, I don't really feel like going through and reading the entire thread first, so I'm just going to jot down what I think first, then come back and scan the rest of the thread, and go from there.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Rework all the Transmutations from the ground up. I've been preparing to play a Demon game, and it strikes me that the demon form you start with? The equivalent to nearly all of Vulcanus and Electification can be taken as a starting character, and only with a portion of your starting abilities. And those aren't the only ones like that. Normally, I wouldn't care about comparing one game to another. But it only highlights how much things are different in Chronicle books in general.<br /> <br /> 2) Increase the number of base refinements to 8 - the seven alchemical metals plus radioactive Uranium. Hints on making other refinements. Not really important, but just something I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 3) Eliminate the Hisil from the base game. There's no call to bringing in an entire new realm into designing this game, nor the troubles and regulations it brings. Especially not when there are plenty of other local spirit phenomenon in Twilight you can deal with instead. The game should focus on the game's own spiritual beings first and foremost. Make the qashmal more important to the game than just plot hooks. <br /> <br /> 4) Reworked Wastelands / options for a city based game. Nomadic life is all well and good, but how about the concentration camp, or the street bum as a Promethean society? Something different than just the same wandering roads would be lovely. <br /> <br /> 5) All the options for alternative creation methods? Born from a statue, or having a human creator, or tulpa made flesh, or Unfleshed, or whatever? Built as an option into the core six humors. In fact, while we're at it, we need to rework the six humors so that the resemble their mythological counterparts more strongly. Frankenstein monster is good. Indeed, the core book pushed that a bit too much. But the golem, the spiritual sacrifice, the work of art, the resurrected dead, and the nuclear zombie should have their own themes stand out a bit more. Promethean is a game about the Created - all the different types of created monsters. <br /> <br /> 6) Related to the above, but a better bane than just &quot;kill it with fire!&quot; It makes zero sense to use fire to kill a golem or tulpa. If anything, human masses are the bane, and I'd like to see that played up instead of just burning them. Like, those with heavy disquiet should hurt a Promethean more, or something similar. Ideally, each of the nine game lines should have a unique bane, imho. <br /> <br /> 7) Rework Humanity. Rename Humanity as well. Humanity was a list of good VS evil acts. Never mind that humanity has its dark side. That we had two (count them, two!) refinements that focused on indulging the darker parts of the human psyche. We need the new Integrity to reflect<br /> <br /> 8) We need an Aura. Vampire has Predator's aura. Mage is getting their nimbus to work like the predator's aura, and hints of a werewolfy one as well. Demons use their cover to spoof - they use an un-aura to hide. Prometheans can have an aura as well. And the fun part? The Aura can directly tie into Disquiet as well as becoming more human. This also makes Disquiet to be something you actively use - not sure on the benefit to the game, other than I think that it will add a bit more weight to the player. Do you push and gain more humanity, or do you sit and wallow and never connect or learn? Not sure if it would really benefit the game, but it seems to work awesome for the Big Three. <br /> <br /> 9) Clones. Core book mentioned them. Work more on it. <br /> <br /> 10) Lairs. More frankenstein monsters with tesla coils. More galatea art studios, or ulgan shrines. Make it happen! <br /> <br /> 11) The default game is to have a Promethean start off as the created monster rebelling against their maker, or whatever. And then, they eventually grow into Pygmalion making his Galatea to fall in love with, or Frankenstein making his monster, or the rabbi trying to make a servant. The makers are supposed to be a huge deal, inspiring Torment into their creations. The whole I Hate You Vampire Dad trope dialed to 11. Needs more attention. Many people I talk to don't even know that its in the core book! <br /> <br /> 12) Better descriptions of some stuff. Going to the wastes - are Prometheans effectively ageless or not? Agg damage and losing limbs. General cleaning up of details. <br /> <br /> 13) I actually like torment as is, so I have no complaints either way. Given the bump to frenzy and werewolf's likely bump to their rage, we'll probably see a boost in power for falling into Torment, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T19:14:47-08:00","id":67574,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on previous comments:<br /> <br /> ~ We don't need a division between Lineage and Humor. Just add more options on Lineage. Rename it if you must. But you don't need to list off separate lineages, especially if we use the option to have mortal demiurges more common and able to make Prometheans, as per the supplement books. Pretty much all the other ways of making Prometheans can just be alternative creation methods for the core six Lineages. But the main groups, no matter what, should still hit the major archetypes of Frank. Monster / Android, Golem, Living Art, Resurrection Man, Spirit Born. The dreamborn tulpa could fit into Ulgan, the unfleshed as Golem or Frankenstein Monster.<br /> <br /> ~ Athanors, rather than push it on Lineage or Refinement, should stand as a true z-axis. As in, a third thing you chose independent of your birth or your philosophy.<br /> <br /> ~ No, don't do the same format as Demons with their Embeds. While the two games have a shit ton in common, I'd like to see more in the way of differences between the splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-07-2014, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T03:00:30-08:00","id":67813,"title":"","content":"Yeah; you do need to split of Lineage and Humour; if nothing else the Branded Throng rules work on Humours not Lineage so with more than 5 Lineages you need to start making Humour explicit. Also; those aren't major archetypes.<br /> <br /> Mind you; I'd like to see Lineage/Humour as a reverse of Seeming/Kith. In that Lineages get a ton of wordcount, while Humours just get a few paragraphs and a tiny bit of mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T07:40:16-08:00","id":67893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67813#post67813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; you do need to split of Lineage and Humour; if nothing else the Branded Throng rules work on Humours not Lineage so with more than 5 Lineages you need to start making Humour explicit. Also; those aren't major archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are no need of more than six (counting the Zeke) lineages/genesis/humor/whatever. Why? Because you don't need the concept of an actual lineage in the game. There are too many options for being created, spontaneously or not. Are you going to have every one being a new lineage? What mechanics would the even need? Torment, Wasteland, and Disquiet are based on humor. All that's left is Bestowment, and just having options to pick from at character creation is all you need.<br /> <br /> Adding &quot;lineage&quot; doesn't really add anything to the game other than complexity for the sake of having complexity.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, yes, those are major archetypes. Living statues that move around - not only weeping angels but cursed dolls or medusa and her statues? Frankenstein's monster? Golems of all ilks? How are they not? Only the Zeke is questionable as an archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-08-2014, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T08:14:17-08:00","id":67903,"title":"","content":"<b>Humour:</b> Torment and Disquiet; associated Element and Wasteland. General information about its temperament. Possibly do a split-page write-up, with the top half of a page detailing a Humour (temperament, Torment, and Disquiet) and the bottom half detailing an Element (Wasteland, possibly hazardous manifestations that can be tapped for healing: e.g., electricity for Fire).<br /> <br /> <b>Lineage:</b> Bestowment, Disfigurements, details for the Generative Act, and stories about its Progenitor. Possibly an Affinity Transmutation set or a preferred Refinement that serves as its \u201cground state\u201d (the way Stannum does for all non-Nuclear Prometheans in the core edition).<br /> <br /> I see two or three sample Lineages being given for each Humour, with a strong implication that they\u2019re <i>just</i> samples, and that players should be encouraged to devise their own, using the existing ones as guidelines \u2014 and yes, I\u2019d use this to encourage \u201cLineages of one\u201d. Since the relationship between Humours and Lineages is one-to-many, listing a Promethean\u2019s Lineage on the character sheet would suffice.<br /> <br /> As for the Transmutations being more like Embeds: my main motivation behind that suggestion was that the pricing scheme for Transmutations is heavily reliant on the escalating costs that GMC got rid of. Transmutations don\u2019t <i>have</i> to have their dot ratings purged; but if they don\u2019t, the only workable alternative (aside from forcing them into purchase chains like Disciplines) would be to price them much like Merits: e.g., a one-dot Transmutation costs one or two Experiences, while a five-dot Transmutation costs five or six Experiences. I really don\u2019t see any other viable options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-08-2014, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T09:58:58-08:00","id":67960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67893#post67893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are no need of more than six (counting the Zeke) lineages/genesis/humor/whatever. Why? Because you don't need the concept of an actual lineage in the game. There are too many options for being created, spontaneously or not. Are you going to have every one being a new lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, why not.<br /> <br /> Though personally I'd introduce the Humour/Lineage split in the corebook but only give the five core Lineages. More can be introduced later down the line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67893#post67893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And, yes, those are major archetypes. Living statues that move around - not only weeping angels but cursed dolls or medusa and her statues? Frankenstein's monster? Golems of all ilks? How are they not? Only the Zeke is questionable as an archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do the Galataids and weeping angles have in common; apart from being made from stone? Because if the answer is nothing then that's not an archetype.<br /> <br /> Now in reality the archetypes for Promethian are not Golems or Frankenstine's Monster. That's just the presentation. The archetypes are fundamental flaws, flaws which are fixed by what you learn on the Pilgrimage. The Galataid's archetype is &quot;needs someone else to feel complete&quot;, and that can be expressed in more ways than just romantic. So one Humour, with a Lineage for romance, maybe another kith for robots that feel without productive work they're worthless. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67903#post67903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lineage:</b> Bestowment, Disfigurements, details for the Generative Act, and stories about its Progenitor. Possibly an Affinity Transmutation set or a preferred Refinement that serves as its \u201cground state\u201d (the way Stannum does for all non-Nuclear Prometheans in the core edition).</div> </div> </div> </div> Throw in construction too - being made of flesh, clay, metal and silicon or nanobots is a Lineage thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T11:23:54-08:00","id":67989,"title":"","content":"I figured that was implicit in \u201cdetails of the generative act\u201d. But yeah; whether you\u2019re a reanimated corpse, an animated figurine, or a self-aware machine certainly is more of a Lineage thing than a Humour thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T23:17:49-08:00","id":68267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the first two, I\u2019m hoping that the Promethean Dark Era will be far enough back in time to justify both \u2014 at least in part. If it\u2019s set prior to the 19th century, it will predate both electricity as a technology and Frankenstein: the former would all but require an overhaul of the Electrification Transmutations, and the latter would require addressing the lack of the Wretched Lineage. </div> </div> </div>I understand it to be 1930's US Dust Bowl. Electricity is pretty widely available, though not ubiquitous; Electrification would still possess its throwback powers, though it would also be on the cutting edge of human technology. It's hard to imagine what pre-electric Electrification might look like, or how it might be conceived as a part of Stannum. Actually, it's a bit odd that Stannum has Electrification while Mercurius has Vulcanus, when it should probably be the other way around, given the &quot;basic&quot; nature of Tin, and the ancient origins of the Created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T06:56:15-08:00","id":68399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataeaver:<br /> Humour:</b> Torment and Disquiet; associated Element and Wasteland. </div> </div> </div>I think Torment and Disquiet should be determined at least as much by Lineage there - specifically, being refelective of the obsession that drove the demiurge to make a Promethean in the first place. Like the Frankenstein Disquiet and Torment are largely about pettiness and spite - you could associate that with choler/fire, but you could also associate it with how Frankenstein's initial rejection of the creature was down to little more than him not being a pretty as Frankenstein had hoped. Meanwhile, choler/fire/anger can express in other ways. <br /> Element and Humour suggest <i>types</i> of Disquiet and Torment, but the specifics are down to Lineage (and in story terms would be the determining factor in which element a particular act of creation aligned to).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Verge:</b><br /> It's hard to imagine what pre-electric Electrification might look like, or how it might be conceived as a part of Stannum. </div> </div> </div>Some of the powers would have to be different, but pre-electric Electrification would be about lightning - which means being reflective of a barely comprehensible force divorced from any human feeling or control - which is a fairly good fit for Stannum.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T07:21:10-08:00","id":68416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67960#post67960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure, why not.<br /> <br /> Though personally I'd introduce the Humour/Lineage split in the corebook but only give the five core Lineages. More can be introduced later down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because it doesn't even really add anything to the game. &quot;Choose a Bestowment,&quot; &quot;choose a method of creation,&quot; and anything else should all be independent choices. Progenitor stories? Zero need for the vast majority of so called &quot;Lineages,&quot; as they're pretty much independently created by modern demiurges. And, hells! There's no reason that you can't have a Frankenstein making several different creations using various methods, and each with a different bestowment!<br /> <br /> Tying it all together sounds neat, but its unnecessary, and not something I would ever suggest in a game. Its not something that's needed - adds complexity in a format that doesn't actually help inspire stories. If anything, it gets in the way of it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do the Galataids and weeping angles have in common; apart from being made from stone? Because if the answer is nothing then that's not an archetype. </div> </div> </div> Being made of stone has nothing to do with it. Its being a work of art that matters. They're designed to be pretty, or terrifying, or captivating somehow when you look at them. They evoke emotion. That's they're purpose. You could be flesh, stone, doesn't matter. Hells, I'd allow plastic. <br /> <br /> Also, note that weeping angels from Doctor Who not only didn't speak, but were silent all the time. Galatea pandorans are the Silent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now in reality the archetypes for Promethian are not Golems or Frankenstine's Monster. That's just the presentation. The archetypes are fundamental flaws, flaws which are fixed by what you learn on the Pilgrimage. The Galataid's archetype is &quot;needs someone else to feel complete&quot;, and that can be expressed in more ways than just romantic. So one Humour, with a Lineage for romance, maybe another kith for robots that feel without productive work they're worthless. Etc. </div> </div> </div> Ummm.... how is that even related to the definition of archetype? That may be a common thread within the archetype, but that has nothing to do with archetypes as a word. Its also a very tiny part of the actual Galatea archetype, and one I'm going to argue ties into the whole art thing above - art is made to be observed and evoke emotion of some kind, as its entire purpose is to have a relationship of some kind with its audience. I'm going to try and avoid a semantics argument, and tell you expressly what I mean.<br /> <br /> Archetypes, as I'm using it, are, &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a recurrent symbol or motif in literature, art, or mythology.&quot; Or you could call it a trope, if you wanted. The point is, archetypes are so much more than just a flaw of some kind. It is something broad.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T07:24:19-08:00","id":68417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68267#post68267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it's a bit odd that Stannum has Electrification while Mercurius has Vulcanus, when it should probably be the other way around, given the &quot;basic&quot; nature of Tin, and the ancient origins of the Created.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suspect it has to do with a frankenstein monster. Electricity is a thing with Frankenstein monsters, and the Tin Frankenstein is as much a stereotype as the Invictus Ventrue is in Requiem, or the Rahu Blood Talon is in Forsaken. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T07:49:14-08:00","id":68427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68416#post68416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because it doesn't even really add anything to the game. &quot;Choose a Bestowment,&quot; &quot;choose a method of creation,&quot; and anything else should all be independent choices. Progenitor stories? Zero need for the vast majority of so called &quot;Lineages,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure it adds something. Long term established lineages makes it clear that the Created are also Creators, that's an enormously important thing.<br /> <br /> There's others, but that's in my opinion the biggest one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68416#post68416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being made of stone has nothing to do with it. Its being a work of art that matters. They're designed to be pretty, or terrifying, or captivating somehow when you look at them. They evoke emotion. That's they're purpose. You could be flesh, stone, doesn't matter. Hells, I'd allow plastic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me make one thing perfectly clear. The Weeping Angels are not works of art. They're naturally born living creatures who happen to turn to stone if someone looks at them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68416#post68416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, note that weeping angels from Doctor Who not only didn't speak, but were silent all the time. Galatea pandorans are the Silent.</div> </div> </div> </div> A mere coincidence. Besides, the Weaping Angels can communicate, just not with vibrations in the air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68416#post68416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ummm.... how is that even related to the definition of archetype?</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't think that <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClingyJealousGirl\" target=\"_blank\">clingy romantic partners</a> are an archetype. What about The Rebel Without a Cause?<br /> <br /> The very core of the Galataids is that they don't feel complete without someone to love them. The fact they are art is merely backstory and justification for that core emotion. Their entire pilgrimage is learning to progress beyond it until they have self respect and can feel complete by themselves. <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the same for the other four Lineages. They each have some archetypical flaw that could be found in dozens of different fictional characters and their pilgrimage is about fixing that flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T14:11:11-08:00","id":68637,"title":"","content":"The Lineages &quot;need&quot; to remain as presented. King's Raven nailed it: Lineages aren't one Demiurge's act, repeated ad nauseam, they are generations of creatures who recreate the original sin out of necessity and identity, and that act is both sacred and profane <i>every time</i>. Furthermore, each and every Demiurge created their primogenitor in an act of divine reverence. Or irreverence. The Demiurges played God, and <i>won</i>.<br /> <br /> That's not to say they are right for every game. But they add more to the game than breaking down their mechanics and saying, &quot;or some dude made you in his basement, whatever&quot;. Prometheans exist in a world where they can trace their existence back to an act looked upon by angels, where the end of Sodom and Gomorrah has a very likely explanation, and where mysteries and and discoveries carry the promise of transmutation of the soul. Lineages ground player characters in that world, where humours do not.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Lineages can be restricting, but there are means to open that up, if a player doesn't <i>want </i>to play what's provided.<br /> <br /> And the Weeping Angels predate the universe. They are creatures who can only live in Heisenbergian Uncertainty, to the point they can't even look at each other, and they feed on potential, which is not unlike what the Pyros crave. Pandorans, clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T01:42:21-08:00","id":68900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=67561#post67561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Rework all the Transmutations from the ground up. I've been preparing to play a Demon game, and it strikes me that the demon form you start with? The equivalent to nearly all of Vulcanus and Electification can be taken as a starting character, and only with a portion of your starting abilities. And those aren't the only ones like that. Normally, I wouldn't care about comparing one game to another. But it only highlights how much things are different in Chronicle books in general.<br /> <br /> 2) Increase the number of base refinements to 8 - the seven alchemical metals plus radioactive Uranium. Hints on making other refinements. Not really important, but just something I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 3) Eliminate the Hisil from the base game. There's no call to bringing in an entire new realm into designing this game, nor the troubles and regulations it brings. Especially not when there are plenty of other local spirit phenomenon in Twilight you can deal with instead. The game should focus on the game's own spiritual beings first and foremost. Make the qashmal more important to the game than just plot hooks.<br /> <br /> 4) Reworked Wastelands / options for a city based game. Nomadic life is all well and good, but how about the concentration camp, or the street bum as a Promethean society? Something different than just the same wandering roads would be lovely.<br /> <br /> 5) All the options for alternative creation methods? Born from a statue, or having a human creator, or tulpa made flesh, or Unfleshed, or whatever? Built as an option into the core six humors. In fact, while we're at it, we need to rework the six humors so that the resemble their mythological counterparts more strongly. Frankenstein monster is good. Indeed, the core book pushed that a bit too much. But the golem, the spiritual sacrifice, the work of art, the resurrected dead, and the nuclear zombie should have their own themes stand out a bit more. Promethean is a game about the Created - all the different types of created monsters.<br /> <br /> 6) Related to the above, but a better bane than just &quot;kill it with fire!&quot; It makes zero sense to use fire to kill a golem or tulpa. If anything, human masses are the bane, and I'd like to see that played up instead of just burning them. Like, those with heavy disquiet should hurt a Promethean more, or something similar. Ideally, each of the nine game lines should have a unique bane, imho.<br /> <br /> 7) Rework Humanity. Rename Humanity as well. Humanity was a list of good VS evil acts. Never mind that humanity has its dark side. That we had two (count them, two!) refinements that focused on indulging the darker parts of the human psyche. We need the new Integrity to reflect<br /> <br /> 8) We need an Aura. Vampire has Predator's aura. Mage is getting their nimbus to work like the predator's aura, and hints of a werewolfy one as well. Demons use their cover to spoof - they use an un-aura to hide. Prometheans can have an aura as well. And the fun part? The Aura can directly tie into Disquiet as well as becoming more human. This also makes Disquiet to be something you actively use - not sure on the benefit to the game, other than I think that it will add a bit more weight to the player. Do you push and gain more humanity, or do you sit and wallow and never connect or learn? Not sure if it would really benefit the game, but it seems to work awesome for the Big Three.<br /> <br /> 9) Clones. Core book mentioned them. Work more on it.<br /> <br /> 10) Lairs. More frankenstein monsters with tesla coils. More galatea art studios, or ulgan shrines. Make it happen!<br /> <br /> 11) The default game is to have a Promethean start off as the created monster rebelling against their maker, or whatever. And then, they eventually grow into Pygmalion making his Galatea to fall in love with, or Frankenstein making his monster, or the rabbi trying to make a servant. The makers are supposed to be a huge deal, inspiring Torment into their creations. The whole I Hate You Vampire Dad trope dialed to 11. Needs more attention. Many people I talk to don't even know that its in the core book!<br /> <br /> 12) Better descriptions of some stuff. Going to the wastes - are Prometheans effectively ageless or not? Agg damage and losing limbs. General cleaning up of details.<br /> <br /> 13) I actually like torment as is, so I have no complaints either way. Given the bump to frenzy and werewolf's likely bump to their rage, we'll probably see a boost in power for falling into Torment, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanna give a response to all this.<br /> <br /> 1) Demon Form is not something equivalent to anything a Promethean has. Embeds and Exploits, yes, but not Demon Form. I would like to see the Uratha get a Gauru form on par with it, though.<br /> <br /> 2)Why Uranium? And why isn't Centimani on this list?<br /> <br /> 3) The Hisil isn't in the base game. Twilight is, and spirits are, but there aren't any paths for a Promethean to visit the spirit world, nor the Underworld, for that matter. So, done!<br /> <br /> 4) I'm not opposed to a society of Prometheans forming, and I think the rules can be tweaked for more anchored play, but I do think Prometheans need a <i>reason</i> to form a society. Their needs aren't hindered or helped by the presence of another Promethean, even in the absence of Disquiet and Wastelands. If you want to keep true to the themes of Promethean, you need to conceive of a society that can still leave its members feeling lonely and isolated. Vampires have this in spades, but they also have needs that force them to clash and scheme.<br /> <br /> 5) I have no love for the construct rules. There's too often an impulse in players, myself included, to try and handwave away the parts of a character's history that are inconvenient or un-fun. This plays into that impulse, to avoid original sin rather than redeeming it.<br /> <br /> 6) Fire is pretty universally a Bane, and it doesn't seem too out of place to leave it as is for Prometheans. As for other Banes, maybe gold or lead? Gold for the mortality they aren't ready for yet? Or lead to which they cannot return and survive?<br /> <br /> 7) This is almost assured.<br /> <br /> 8) I can't think of a way to make Disquiet an advantage on par with Predator's Aura, except in cases where the Promethean might <i>want</i> to inflict Disquiet. PA is essentially kept on a short leash until the vamp is ready to use it, while Disquiet is already loose in the world and slowly stalking the Promethean. It's hard to turn that into a positive that still underlines the Promethean Condition. <br /> <br /> 9) What more needs to be said? <br /> <br /> 10) Lairs would only benefit from expansion if the game gets a localized option.<br /> <br /> 11) I don't know if I'd characterize it the same way. To be honest, my take is that those conflicts are incidental. Dramatic and interesting, but hardly the default option. Makers don't have to stick around, and often don't, and while their effect on their children is antagonistic, it's not a necessary component of the game to be at loggerheads. I don't think that I'd introduce more rules to make it more &quot;core&quot;.<br /> <br /> 12) Yes, this please.<br /> <br /> s13) I want Torment to be more unified with Disquiet and Wastelands. A Promethean's Torment is very similar to the Disquiet he inflicts (save for maybe the Tammuz), or at least complementary. I would not bump up stats for its duration, simply because we're talking about something more subtle than a psychotic break. A frenzy is a murder fit, while Torment is akin to falling off the wagon. It's giving into addictive behavior, rather than a loss of all impulse control, and I'd bring it in line with Condition mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:50:42-08:00","id":69001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3053-the-long-journey-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-promethean-s-chronicle-book?p=68900#post68900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Demon Form is not something equivalent to anything a Promethean has. Embeds and Exploits, yes, but not Demon Form. I would like to see the Uratha get a Gauru form on par with it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> The point was that its something a starting character has access to. How is unimportant; what is important is fact that Prometheans who all but master Electrification are matched by one ability another splat is taking at starting level. This is the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2)Why Uranium? And why isn't Centimani on this list? </div> </div> </div> The Refinement of Flux is Uranium. Radioactive. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) The Hisil isn't in the base game. Twilight is, and spirits are, but there aren't any paths for a Promethean to visit the spirit world, nor the Underworld, for that matter. So, done! </div> </div> </div> False. The Ulgan's wasteland destroys the Gauntlet. This is wasteland is meaningless unless the Hisil exists. The game assumes that it must in order for it to function. <br /> <br /> The reliance on the Shadow, and the spirits that come from it, need to be excised from the core game. Optional, sure. Default, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) I'm not opposed to a society of Prometheans forming, and I think the rules can be tweaked for more anchored play, but I do think Prometheans need a <i>reason</i> to form a society. Their needs aren't hindered or helped by the presence of another Promethean, even in the absence of Disquiet and Wastelands. If you want to keep true to the themes of Promethean, you need to conceive of a society that can still leave its members feeling lonely and isolated. Vampires have this in spades, but they also have needs that force them to clash and scheme. </div> </div> </div> Thus, the suggestion for one based on being scavangers and the homeless poor. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) I have no love for the construct rules. There's too often an impulse in players, myself included, to try and handwave away the parts of a character's history that are inconvenient or un-fun. This plays into that impulse, to avoid original sin rather than redeeming it. </div> </div> </div> Agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Fire is pretty universally a Bane, and it doesn't seem too out of place to leave it as is for Prometheans. </div> </div> </div> Unfleshed? Being horribly damaged by fire? A stone golem? Yeah, no, not seeing it at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10) Lairs would only benefit from expansion if the game gets a localized option. </div> </div> </div> Well, more mad alchemy needs to happen one way or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11) I don't know if I'd characterize it the same way. To be honest, my take is that those conflicts are incidental. Dramatic and interesting, but hardly the default option. Makers don't have to stick around, and often don't, and while their effect on their children is antagonistic, it's not a necessary component of the game to be at loggerheads. I don't think that I'd introduce more rules to make it more &quot;core&quot;. </div> </div> </div> Makers are a major source of torment by the core book. They're supposed to be a big deal at first. And yet, they get brushed over. Relationships with makers are supposed to be a huge part of Frankenstein's story, as well as Galatea's and the Golem of Prague's. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:40:52-08:00","id":69262,"title":"","content":"Demon Form isn't a problem: it's not the same game. Also, this is true for most of the demon's form powers anyway, in that they they often duplicate another splat's full discipline range. And that's going to happen in a system where fx aren't rated in dots. Prometheans are trying to stay one step ahead of Disquiet, while demons are trying to outrun God. Different power scales are features of the game.<br /> <br /> And while Ulgans might tear holes in the world, it's not the same as stepping sideways. The Shadow isn't detailed, there are no rules for crossing over, and Ulgan Wastelands take months to get to stage 4. There is no &quot;reliance&quot; on it, but the details on spirits are there just in case the Riven show up in your chronicle. And you can have a fully operational game without the Riven.<br /> <br /> Ah, Unfleshed and stone Golems are things I'm against as being part of a new core book. Unfleshed aren't any more proofed against fire than cars are, as lubricants, plastics, and fuels are all flammable. Clay Golems (as is traditional) might be fired too much. I'm not sure making the Prometheans even tougher is a necessity, in any case.<br /> <br /> While the Maker-Created conflict is significant, it's not mandatory, and in a scattered society of damaged pariahs, it's a luxury. Deadbeat dads and missing moms are the norm. While a few more paragraphs on be-there makers would be welcome, insisting on the tumult only constrains the game. Myself, I wish they would put more emphasis on interacting with the lives of the bodies the Created inhabit, but that's just as case-by-case as daddy issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:28:01-08:00","id":69349,"title":"","content":"On a tangent to the existing conversation... the God-Machine is a small fraction of potential interactions and can be mitigated by acting in accordance to one's Cover. A fatal flaw in the Disquiet system is the globality of its effects and that there is really no way of mitigating it other than being nomadic. Unlike other nWoD games, this locks the storyteller into very specific types of Chronicles. If I don't want to run a cross-country Chronicle I shouldn't be essentially shut out from using the Promethean game as a basis for my Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Curtailing both Disquiet and Wasteland effects to more sane levels for troupe play would be very helpful. I've already done such things for my own games through house rules. If Disquiet scoped more like a Demon &quot;going loud&quot; and Cover breaches then overall playability of Promethean would be increased. Of course YMMV on how you define &quot;playability.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T15:23:56-08:00","id":73413,"title":"","content":"The thing I want more than anything is for them to drop the &quot;It's mostly Prometheans creating new Prometheans.&quot; Scatter the setting with mortal demiurges - Frankenstein was the first to use <i>that particular method</i>, but he wasn't the last. An obsessed sculptor can recreate a Galateid in some decrepit artist's hovel in 1985 New York. <br /> <br /> Some additional lineages would be nice. Just drawing from mythology, I could see Talos, Zombie, and Tulpa working just fine. Tulpa's could be created by communities acting as group demiurges, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Play around with the creation myths, basically. Prometheans have an intrinsically mutable condition and pilgrimage, it stands to reason it would be just as varied and mutable throughout their history. No need for radioactive monsters to be the only fun modern demiurges are having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T14:47:57-07:00","id":141824,"title":"","content":"This just in from rpg.net's <b>Promethean: the Created, updated with GMC</b> thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Hey, this suddenly became relevant to me.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlackHat_Matt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Cause of this book I'm outlining. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}